 the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=(-6)\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-5)=3\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -(-5) & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2/3 & -1 \\\\ 5/3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186297547 :question/problem "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |" "Calculate ${A}^{-1},$ where\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186297547 :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=5\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0=-10\n$$\n\nUsing the for