- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299564 :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}19 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}19 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299565 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T,$ find $T(v).$\n\n| $T(v)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |" "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T,$ find $T(v).$\n\n| $T(v)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299565 :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299566 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T,$ find $T(v).$\n\n| $T(v)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |" "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIf $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T,$ find $T(v).$\n\n| $T(v)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299566 :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299567 :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-5y+7x \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-5y+7x \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299567 :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7x-5y \\\\ -4x+2y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299568 :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}4x+7y \\\\ 8y-5x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{fiel