 -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(1)(-3)-(2)(-1)}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3+2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299614 :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation.\n\nThe variable $x$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ Similarly, the variable $y$ does not appear in the second equation, which means that its coefficient is $0$ too. So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0x+8y=-8 \\\\ -4x+0y=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin