egin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 14 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}].$" "Here, $A$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}={AB}_{4\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 9 \\\\ ∗ & 14 \\\\ 5 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,2=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ ∗ & 9 \\\\ ∗ & 14 \\\\ 5 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 \\\\ ∗ & 14 \\\\ 5 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,0=0\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 14 \\\\ 5 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-1=(-1)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 14 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-4=5\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 14 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186299651 :question/problem "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $9$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $9$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299651 :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & -8\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-3=1\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 9 & -8\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-8=0\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0+4\\cdot (-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 9 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & -8\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-3=1\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 \\\\ 9 & -8\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-8=0\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0+4\\cdot (-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 \\\\ 9 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299652 :question/problem "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299652 :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,5=2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 5 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,7=4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,5=2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 5 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,7=4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299653 :question/problem "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-6$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $11$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-6$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $11$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299653 :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -2\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-2=4\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -2\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-2=4\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -6 \\\\ 11 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299659 :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $u$ onto $v.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,u=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" "Let $u=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the vector projection of $u$ onto $v.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,u=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$"] [:db/cas 17592186299660 :question/problem "If $c=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 2k \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ $d=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ and $c⊥d,$ then $k=${{field-1}}." "If $c=\\begin{bmatri