n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |" "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix},$\nthen\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299676 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot (-3)+(-2)\\cdot 5 & 3\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot 5 & (-1)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9+(-10) & 6+2 \\\\ 3+20 & -2+(-4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-19 & 8 \\\\ 23 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\cdot (-3)+(-2)\\cdot 5 & 3\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot 5 & (-1)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9+(-10) & 6+2 \\\\ 3+20 & -2+(-4)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-19 & 8 \\\\ 23 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299677 :question/problem "If $C=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 2 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],$\nthen\n\n| $CD=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |" "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 2 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},$\nthen\n\n| $CD=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299677 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 2 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-3)+(-\\frac{3}{4})\\cdot 1\\, & \\,\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}+(-\\frac{3}{4})\\cdot 4 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-3)+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1\\, & \\,2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{3}{4}\\, & \\,\\frac{5}{4}-3 \\\\ -6+\\frac{1}{3}\\, & \\,5+\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{9}{4} & -\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{17}{3} & \\frac{19}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 2 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-3)+(-\\frac{3}{4})\\cdot 1\\, & \\,\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}+(-\\frac{3}{4})\\cdot 4 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-3)+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1\\, & \\,2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{3}{4}\\, & \\,\\frac{5}{4}-3 \\\\ -6+\\frac{1}{3}\\, & \\,5+\\frac{4}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{9}{4} & -\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{17}{3} & \\frac{19}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299678 :question/problem "If $C=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & 2 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 15 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}],$\nthen\n\n| $CD=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |" "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & 2 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 15 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix},$\nthen\n\n| $CD=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299678 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & 2 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 & 15 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 10+2\\cdot 3\\, & \\,\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 15+2\\cdot 6 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 10+\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 3\\, & \\,(-1)\\cdot 15+\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6+6\\, & \\,9+12 \\\\ -10+4\\, & \\,-15+8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 21 \\\\ -6 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & 2 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 15 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 10+2\\cdot 3\\, & \\,\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 15+2\\cdot 6 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 10+\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 3\\, & \\,(-1)\\cdot 15+\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6+6\\, & \\,9+12 \\\\ -10+4\\, & \\,-15+8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 21 \\\\ -6 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299679 :question/problem "Let $F=GH.$ What is the value of ${f}_{21}$, if\n\n$$\nG=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,H=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\n${f}_{21}=$ \n{{field-1}}" "Let $F=GH.$ What is the value of ${f}_{21}$, if\n\n$$\nG=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,H=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n${f}_{21}=$ \n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299679 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $2$nd row in $G$ by the $1$st column in $H$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{21} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15-2 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying the $2$nd row in $G$ by the $1$st column in $H$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{21} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15-2 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299680 :question/problem "Let $G=HM.$ What is the value of ${g}_{31}$, if\n\n$$\nH=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,M=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\n${g}_{31}=$ \n{{field-1}}" "Let $G=HM.$ What is the value of ${g}_{31}$, if\n\n$$\nH=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,M=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n${g}_{31}=$ \n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299680 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $H$ by the $1$st column in $M$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{31} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-3+15+0+0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $H$ by the $1$st column in $M$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{31} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-3+15+0+0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299681 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0+0+0 & 3+0+0 & 6+0+0 \\\\ 0+6+4 & -1-4+0 & -2+0+12 \\\\ 0+15-2 & 0-10+0 & 0+0-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 13 & -10 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0+0+0 & 3+0+0 & 6+0+0 \\\\ 0+6+4 & -1-4+0 & -2+0+12 \\\\ 0+15-2 & 0-10+0 & 0+0-6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 13 & -10 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299682 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3+3+4 & 6-1+2 & 3+2+0 \\\\ 4-3+10 & 8+1+5 & 4-2+0 \\\\ 2+0+6 & 4+0+3 & 2+0+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 11 & 14 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3+3+4 & 6-1+2 & 3+2+0 \\\\ 4-3+10 & 8+1+5 & 4-2+0 \\\\ 2+0+6 & 4+0+3 & 2+0+0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 11 & 14 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299683 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0+2 & 4+0+1 & 2+0+3 \\\\ 3-3+8 & 6+0+4 & 3-2+12 \\\\ 0+6+10 & 0+0+5 & 0+4+15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 10 & 13 \\\\ 16 & 5 & 19\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2+0+2 & 4+0+1 & 2+0+3 \\\\ 3-3+8 & 6+0+4 & 3-2+12 \\\\ 0+6+10 & 0+0+5 & 0+4+15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 10 & 13 \\\\ 16 & 5 & 19\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299685 :question/problem "Let $P=QR.$ What is the value of ${p}_{31}$, if\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\n${p}_{31}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Let $P=QR.$ What is the value of ${p}_{31}$, if\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n${p}_{31}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299685 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $Q$ by the $1$st column in $R$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}_{31} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2(5)+1(-3)+(-2)(1) \\\\  & =10-3-2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $Q$ by the $1$st column in $R$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}_{31} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2(5)+1(-3)+(-2)(1) \\\\  & =10-3-2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299686 :question/problem "Let $X=YZ.$ What is the value of ${x}_{12}$, if\n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\n${x}_{12}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Let $X=YZ.$ What is the value of ${x}_{12}$, if\n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n${x}_{12}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299686 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $1$st row in $Y$ by the $2$nd column in $Z$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-2)(5)+3(-3)+0(1) \\\\  & =-10-9+0 \\\\  & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying the $1$st row in $Y$ by the $2$nd column in $Z$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)(5)+3(-3)+0(1) \\\\  & =-10-9+0 \\\\  & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299687 :question/problem "Let $Z=XY.$ What is the value of ${z}_{24}$, if\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\n${z}_{24}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Let $Z=XY.$ What is the value of ${z}_{24}$, if\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n${z}_{24}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299687 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $2$nd row in $X$ by the $4$th column in $Y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}_{24} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3(-3)+2(2) \\\\  & =-9+4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying the $2$nd row in $X$ by the $4$th column in $Y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}_{24} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =3(-3)+2(2) \\\\  & =-9+4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299688 :question/problem "If\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}],$\nfind $AB.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $AB.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299688 :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,5=5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -15 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-15=5\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,-2=-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,6=-2\\cdot (-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,5=5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-15=5\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-2=-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,6=-2\\cdot (-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186299689 :question/problem "Find $PQ,$ if\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $PQ=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |" "Find $PQ,$ if\n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $PQ=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299689 :question/worked-solution "Here, $P$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix and $Q$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $P$ and $1$ row in matrix $Q$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{P}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Q}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={PQ}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot (-4) & 0\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-4) & 3\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-4) & (-1)\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Here, $P$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix and $Q$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $P$ and $1$ row in matrix $Q$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{P}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Q}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={PQ}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0\\cdot (-4) & 0\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-4) & 3\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-4) & (-1)\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299690 :question/problem "If \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}b & a & -b \\\\ -b & a & b \\\\ -b & 0 & -b\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$x=[\\begin{aligned}-b \\\\ 0 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],$\nfind $Ax.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Ax=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "If \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}b & a & -b \\\\ -b & a & b \\\\ -b & 0 & -b\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$x=\\begin{bmatrix}-b \\\\ 0 \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $Ax.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Ax=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299690 :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}b & a & -b \\\\ -b & a & b \\\\ -b & 0 & -b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-b \\\\ 0 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (-b) & + & a\\cdot 0 & + & (-b)\\cdot b \\\\ (-b)\\cdot (-b) & + & a\\cdot 0 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,b\\cdot b \\\\ (-b)\\cdot (-b) & + & 0\\cdot 0 & + & (-b)\\cdot b\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-{b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & (-{b}^{2}) \\\\ {b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & {b}^{2} \\\\ {b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & (-{b}^{2})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{b}^{2} \\\\ 2{b}^{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =\\begin{bmatrix}b & a & -b \\\\ -b & a & b \\\\ -b & 0 & -b\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-b \\\\ 0 \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (-b) & + & a\\cdot 0 & + & (-b)\\cdot b \\\\ (-b)\\cdot (-b) & + & a\\cdot 0 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,b\\cdot b \\\\ (-b)\\cdot (-b) & + & 0\\cdot 0 & + & (-b)\\cdot b\\end{aligned}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{aligned}-{b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & (-{b}^{2}) \\\\ {b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & {b}^{2} \\\\ {b}^{2} & + & 0 & + & (-{b}^{2})\\end{aligned}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2{b}^{2} \\\\ 2{b}^{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299691 :question/problem "If \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}m & n & -m \\\\ m & -n & -m \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ p \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$\nfind $Pu.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Pu=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "If \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}m & n & -m \\\\ m & -n & -m \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$u=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ p \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $Pu.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Pu=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299691 :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pu & =[\\begin{aligned}m & n & -m \\\\ m & -n & -m \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ p \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m\\cdot 1 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,n\\cdot p & + & (-m)\\cdot 1 \\\\ m\\cdot 1 & + & (-n)\\cdot p & + & (-m)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 0\\cdot 1 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\cdot p & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,np & + & (-m) \\\\ m & + & (-np) & + & (-m) \\\\ 0 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2p & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}np \\\\ -np \\\\ 2p\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pu & =\\begin{bmatrix}m & n & -m \\\\ m & -n & -m \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ p \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{aligned}m\\cdot 1 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,n\\cdot p & + & (-m)\\cdot 1 \\\\ m\\cdot 1 & + & (-n)\\cdot p & + & (-m)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 0\\cdot 1 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\cdot p & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{aligned}m & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,np & + & (-m) \\\\ m & + & (-np) & + & (-m) \\\\ 0 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2p & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}np \\\\ -np \\\\ 2p\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299692 :question/problem "Find $By$  if \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}6p & -4q \\\\ -5p & 2q\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$y=[\\begin{aligned}p \\\\ q\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $By=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "Find $By$  if \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}6p & -4q \\\\ -5p & 2q\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$y=\\begin{bmatrix}p \\\\ q\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $By=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299692 :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}By & =[\\begin{aligned}6p & -4q \\\\ -5p & 2q\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}p \\\\ q\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}6p\\cdot p & + & (-4q)\\cdot q \\\\ -5p\\cdot p & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2q\\cdot q\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6{p}^{2}-4{q}^{2} \\\\ -5{p}^{2}+2{q}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}By & =\\begin{bmatrix}6p & -4q \\\\ -5p & 2q\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}p \\\\ q\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{aligned}6p\\cdot p & + & (-4q)\\cdot q \\\\ -5p\\cdot p & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2q\\cdot q\\end{aligned}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6{p}^{2}-4{q}^{2} \\\\ -5{p}^{2}+2{q}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299694 :question/problem "Find $Nz$ if\n$N=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$z=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Nz=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "Find $Nz$ if\n$N=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$z=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Nz=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299694 :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Nz & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}(-8)\\cdot 3 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,1\\cdot (-4) & + & 2\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot 3 & + & (-6)\\cdot (-4) & + & 5\\cdot 2 \\\\ 4\\cdot 3 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\cdot (-4) & + & 7\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-24 & + & (-4) & + & 4 \\\\ 9 & + & \\,\\,\\,24 & + & 10 \\\\ 12 & + & (-8) & + & 14\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 \\\\ 43 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Nz & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{aligned}(-8)\\cdot 3 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,1\\cdot (-4) & + & 2\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot 3 & + & (-6)\\cdot (-4) & + & 5\\cdot 2 \\\\ 4\\cdot 3 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\cdot (-4) & + & 7\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{aligned}-24 & + & (-4) & + & 4 \\\\ 9 & + & \\,\\,\\,24 & + & 10 \\\\ 12 & + & (-8) & + & 14\\end{aligned}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-24 \\\\ 43 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299695 :question/problem "Compute the following:\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |" "Compute the following:\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299695 :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-4\\cdot 3 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6\\cdot (-1) & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\cdot 4 \\\\ 5\\cdot 3 & + & (-3)\\cdot (-1) & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,7\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1\\cdot 3 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8\\cdot (-1) & + & (-2)\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 & + & (-6) & + & 8 \\\\ 15 & + & 3 & + & 28 \\\\ 3 & + & (-8) & + & (-8)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 46 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{aligned}-4\\cdot 3 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6\\cdot (-1) & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\cdot 4 \\\\ 5\\cdot 3 & + & (-3)\\cdot (-1) & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,7\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1\\cdot 3 & + & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8\\cdot (-1) & + & (-2)\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & + & (-6) & + & 8 \\\\ 15 & + & 3 & + & 28 \\\\ 3 & + & (-8) & + & (-8)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 46 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299698 :question/problem "Compute the following:\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}0 & 11 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "Compute the following:\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 11 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299698 :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 11 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 5+11\\cdot (-1) \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 11 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 11 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 11 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0\\cdot 5+11\\cdot (-1) \\\\ ∗\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ ∗\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 11 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 11 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299699 :question/problem "Compute the following:\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "Compute the following:\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299699 :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(-7)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-34 \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-34 \\\\ 5\\cdot 4+8\\cdot (-2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-34 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-34 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-7)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\ ∗\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-34 \\\\ ∗\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-34 \\\\ 5\\cdot 4+8\\cdot (-2)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-34 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-34 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299700 :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${B}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${B}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299700 :question/worked-solution "We write down $B$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $B$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${B}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{B}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "We write down $B$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $B$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${B}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{B}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299715 :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."] [:db/cas 17592186299716 :question/problem "For the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{33}$ of the entry ${b}_{33}.$\n\n${M}_{33}=${{field-1}}" "For the matrix\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind the minor ${M}_{33}$ of the entry ${b}_{33}.$\n\n${M}_{33}=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299716 :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${b}_{33}=6$ (third row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $6$ are removed: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & -1 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{33}=6$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{33} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2-5 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The minor of ${b}_{33}=6$ (third row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $6$ are removed: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & -1 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{33}=6$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{33} & =\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2-5 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299717 :question/problem "For the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the entry ${a}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}" "For the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the entry ${a}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299717 :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${a}_{23}=-1$ (second row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-1$ are removed: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{23}=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6-(-4)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =12-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The minor of ${a}_{23}=-1$ (second row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-1$ are removed: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{23}=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6-(-4)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =12-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299718 :question/problem "For the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{22}$ of the entry ${b}_{22}.$\n\n${M}_{22}=${{field-1}}" "For the matrix\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$\nfind the minor ${M}_{22}$ of the entry ${b}_{22}.$\n\n${M}_{22}=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299718 :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${b}_{22}=0$ (second row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $0$ are removed: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ & -3 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{22}=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{22} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 6-(-3)\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =6-(-21) \\\\  & =6+21 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The minor of ${b}_{22}=0$ (second row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $0$ are removed: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & ∗ & -3 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{22}=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{22} & =\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 6-(-3)\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =6-(-21) \\\\  & =6+21 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299719 :question/problem "For the matrix\n$Y=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{32}$ of the entry ${y}_{32}.$\n\n${M}_{32}=${{field-1}}" "For the matrix\n$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nfind the minor ${M}_{32}$ of the entry ${y}_{32}.$\n\n${M}_{32}=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299719 :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${y}_{32}=-1$ (third row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-1$ are removed: \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ ∗ & -1 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${y}_{32}=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{32} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =0-15 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The minor of ${y}_{32}=-1$ (third row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-1$ are removed: \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ ∗ & -1 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${y}_{32}=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{32} & =\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =0-15 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299720 :question/problem "For the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{12}$ of the entry ${c}_{12}.$\n\n${M}_{12}=${{field-1}}" "For the matrix\n$C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$\nfind the minor ${M}_{12}$ of the entry ${c}_{12}.$\n\n${M}_{12}=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299720 :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ (first row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{12} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot 6-4\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =0-28 \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ (first row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{12} & =\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 6-4\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =0-28 \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299721 :question/problem "For the matrix\n$F=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & v & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{13}$ of the element ${f}_{13}.$\n\n${M}_{13}=${{field-1}}" "For the matrix\n$F=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & v & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind the minor ${M}_{13}$ of the element ${f}_{13}.$\n\n${M}_{13}=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299721 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${f}_{13},$ we remove the first row and third column: \n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & -2 \\\\ 3 & v & ∗ \\\\ 5 & 6 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${f}_{13}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{13} & =det[\\begin{aligned}3 & v \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & v \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6-v\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =18-5v\\end{aligned}\n$$" "To evaluate the minor of ${f}_{13},$ we remove the first row and third column: \n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ & -2 \\\\ 3 & v & ∗ \\\\ 5 & 6 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${f}_{13}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{13} & =det\\begin{bmatrix}3 & v \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & v \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6-v\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =18-5v\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299722 :question/problem "$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}y & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $y$ in the matrix above.\n\n$y=$\n {{field-1}}" "$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}y & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $y$ in the matrix above.\n\n$y=$\n {{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299722 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${f}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}y & ∗ & 1 \\\\ 2 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =y\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4y-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-2 & =10 \\\\ 4y & =12 \\\\ y & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=3.$" "To evaluate the minor of ${f}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}y & ∗ & 1 \\\\ 2 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =y\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4y-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-2 & =10 \\\\ 4y & =12 \\\\ y & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=3.$"] [:db/cas 17592186299723 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $x$ in the matrix above.\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}" "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $x$ in the matrix above.\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299723 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}x & ∗ & 3 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & =x\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-12 & =10 \\\\ 6x & =22 \\\\ x & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{3}.$" "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}x & ∗ & 3 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & =x\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-12 & =10 \\\\ 6x & =22 \\\\ x & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{3}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186299724 :question/problem "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & r & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is $15$, find the value of $r$ in the matrix above.\n\n$r=$\n {{field-1}}" "$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & r & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is $15$, find the value of $r$ in the matrix above.\n\n$r=$\n {{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299724 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${b}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & r & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & r \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}] & =1\\cdot 8-r\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =8-7r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is $15$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-7r & =15 \\\\ -7r & =7 \\\\ r & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $r=-1.$" "To evaluate the minor of ${b}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & r & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & r \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & =1\\cdot 8-r\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =8-7r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is $15$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-7r & =15 \\\\ -7r & =7 \\\\ r & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $r=-1.$"] [:db/cas 17592186299725 :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & p & 7 \\\\ 6 & -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $p$ are\n\n$p=$ \n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,p=$\n{{field-2}}." "Given that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & p & 7 \\\\ 6 & -8 & p-15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $p$ are\n\n$p=$ \n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,p=$\n{{field-2}}."] [:db/cas 17592186299725 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & p & 7 \\\\ ∗ & -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =p(p-15)-7(-8) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}-15p+56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}-15p+56 & =0 \\\\ (p-7)(p-8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=7$ and $p=8.$" "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & p & 7 \\\\ ∗ & -8 & p-15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}\\begin{bmatrix}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =p(p-15)-7(-8) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}-15p+56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}-15p+56 & =0 \\\\ (p-7)(p-8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=7$ and $p=8.$"] [:db/cas 17592186299727 :question/problem "For the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2p & q & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4p & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 2q\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the element ${b}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}" "For the matrix\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2p & q & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4p & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 2q\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the element ${b}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299727 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${b}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2p & q & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =det[\\begin{aligned}2p & q \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2p & q \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2p)\\cdot 7-q\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =14p-6q.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "To evaluate the minor of ${b}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2p & q & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =det\\begin{bmatrix}2p & q \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2p & q \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2p)\\cdot 7-q\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =14p-6q.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299728 :question/problem "For the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & x & 3 \\\\ y & 5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2y & x\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the element ${p}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}" "For the matrix\n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & x & 3 \\\\ y & 5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2y & x\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the element ${p}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299728 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${p}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & x & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2y & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${p}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & 2y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & 2y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (2y)-x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4y-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "To evaluate the minor of ${p}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & x & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2y & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${p}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =det\\begin{bmatrix}2 & x \\\\ 1 & 2y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & x \\\\ 1 & 2y\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (2y)-x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4y-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299733 :question/problem "For the matrix\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & e & f \\\\ 5 & 3d & 2 \\\\ 4 & 7 & d\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{31}$ of the element ${t}_{31}.$\n\n${M}_{31}=${{field-1}}" "For the matrix\n$T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & e & f \\\\ 5 & 3d & 2 \\\\ 4 & 7 & d\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind the minor ${M}_{31}$ of the element ${t}_{31}.$\n\n${M}_{31}=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299733 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${t}_{31},$ we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & e & f \\\\ ∗ & 3d & 2 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${t}_{31}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{31} & =det[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ 3d & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ 3d & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =e\\cdot 2-f\\cdot (3d) \\\\  & =2e-3df.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "To evaluate the minor of ${t}_{31},$ we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & e & f \\\\ ∗ & 3d & 2 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${t}_{31}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{31} & =det\\begin{bmatrix}e & f \\\\ 3d & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}e & f \\\\ 3d & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =e\\cdot 2-f\\cdot (3d) \\\\  & =2e-3df.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299734 :question/problem "For the matrix\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}j & 1 & 3i \\\\ 2 & k & 5 \\\\ 4 & j & k\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{21}$ of the element ${v}_{21}.$\n\n${M}_{21}=${{field-1}}" "For the matrix\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}j & 1 & 3i \\\\ 2 & k & 5 \\\\ 4 & j & k\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind the minor ${M}_{21}$ of the element ${v}_{21}.$\n\n${M}_{21}=${{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299734 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${v}_{21},$ we remove the second row and first column:\n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & 3i \\\\ 2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & j & k\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${v}_{21}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{21} & =det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3i \\\\ j & k\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3i \\\\ j & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot k-(3i)\\cdot j \\\\  & =k-3ij.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "To evaluate the minor of ${v}_{21},$ we remove the second row and first column:\n\n$$\nV=\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & 1 & 3i \\\\ 2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & j & k\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${v}_{21}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{21} & =det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3i \\\\ j & k\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3i \\\\ j & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot k-(3i)\\cdot j \\\\  & =k-3ij.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299735 :question/problem "Given that $c=2i-5j+k$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ find $4c-3d.$\n\n$4c-3d=⟨$\n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}},\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" "Given that $c=2i-5j+k$ and $d=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},$ find $4c-3d.$\n\n$4c-3d=⟨$\n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}},\n{{field-3}}$⟩$"] [:db/cas 17592186299735 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\nc=2i-5j+k=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute $4c-3d,$ we need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4c-3d & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -23 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =⟨-4,-23,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, notice that\n\n$$\nc=2i-5j+k=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo compute $4c-3d,$ we need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4c-3d & =4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -23 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨-4,-23,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299739 :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299740 :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ x \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ x \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299747 :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-5.$\n\n|  |  | $-17$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | $12$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n|  |  | $-3$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |" "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-5.$\n\n|  |  | $-17$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | $12$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n|  |  | $-3$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299747 :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-17 & -12 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 12 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & -12 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 12 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299749 :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-4.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\,$ |  | $4$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |\n|  |  | $7$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |" "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-4.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\,$ |  | $4$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |\n|  |  | $7$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299749 :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\e