& 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 11 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -11 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 11 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -11 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299753 :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | $-3$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ {{field-2}} |  | $-1$ | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |" "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | $-3$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ {{field-2}} |  | $-1$ | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299753 :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =(-3)|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)(2-3)-0(\\,-2-(-3)\\,)+(-3+3) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 