\\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299754 :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299756 :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{12}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n${a}_{12}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186299757 :question/problem 