\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299902 :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 4}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299903 :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299904 :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-y=5 \\\\ x+3y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligne